===== Debricking =====
Follow the [[:toh:mikrotik:common#netboot_of_openwrt_uses_dhcpbootptftp|MikroTik netboot procedure]] documented on the wiki. <del>You need to the hacked RouterBOOT binary to be able to boot OpenWrt (see [[https://github.com/adron-s/openwrt-rb5009#the-installation-process-for-mikrotik-rb5009=|instructions]] by adron-s).</del>

Recovery (from the commit message):

In case you need to reinstall OpenWrt if it crashes after U-Boot, there is a recovery mechanism in OpenWrt to boot the OpenWrt initramfs.\\ You need to hold the reset button while U-Boot is booting and then it will boot the OpenWrt initramfs from:\\
1. USB\\
2. Networking\\ \\ In recovery mode U-Boot will light all of the LED-s except for the switch ones.\\ \\ In case you want to return to RouterOS, you can simply do that via Netinstall like on any other MikroTik board.

